{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjois-Savo lags in crude multidisciplinary team recording at 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9) versus 6.0% nationally, which measures recording practice rather than care.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded",
        "bs:coverage:MDT"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "In the 2019–2023 cohort, the county's crude curative treatment share is 24.5% (95% CI 21.3–28.0; n=157/641) beside 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally, so the 95% confidence interval includes the national value and is not distinguishable from it.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because treatment categories overlap and a patient can receive several, the county's crude life-prolonging share of 38.7% (95% CI 35.0–42.5; n=248/641) versus 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally and crude symptomatic share of 51.2% (95% CI 47.3–55.0; n=328/641) versus 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally have 95% confidence intervals that exclude and lie above the national benchmarks.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:symptomatic:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The county's crude multidisciplinary team recording share of 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9; n=1/641) has a 95% confidence interval that excludes and lies below the 6.0% (893/14873) national figure, even though the KYS regional pathway document states that KYS reviews every patient weekly, because HILMO captures specialised care procedures only from direct patient contacts.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "reg:mdt_practice",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At the national level, preliminary, unpublished figures show an average of 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland alongside 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark, with patient delay averaging 56 days, primary care 41 days, and specialist care 58 days as the longest stage.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjois-Savo's crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 19.3% (95% CI 16.5–22.6) versus 27.5% nationally, consistent with relatively complete recording, though county shares are unadjusted.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:no_treatment_record",
        "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Mixing untreated patients and unrecorded treatment, the crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 19.3% (95% CI 16.5–22.6; n=124/641), its 95% confidence interval lying below 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally; as an inference, not a finding, this is consistent with relatively complete treatment recording, so a low curative share is less likely to be only a recording artefact.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Taulukko 11 gives crude county shares with separate limitations: they are not age-adjusted (age-adjusted shares appear only in Kuva 16 by sex, with digitised ±0.5 percentage point national curative reference lines at 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women), and separately they cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article found that hospital discharge register (HILMO) diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, but this concerns diagnosis concordance only and says nothing about how completely treatment, referrals, or multidisciplinary team meetings are recorded.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure symptoms or referrals by county, primary care visits are not included in the report's data, occupational health is not mentioned, imaging appears only indirectly as clinical-only diagnosis in approximately 20% of patients, and specialist visit (93.6% nationally within 12 months) and treatment records omit exact start dates.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drugs, and multidisciplinary meetings, tracking access times under THL guidance Ohjaus 21/2016 with handover alerts, and naming a diagnostic contact.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:fc81032a80",
        "q:950a2f797b"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and multidisciplinary coding as data-quality signals, given Pohjois-Savo's crude 0.2% (95% CI 0.0–0.9; n=1/641) multidisciplinary record share versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally despite the KYS regional pathway document's weekly review rule, about 48% missing stage data, and incomplete national reporting requiring uniform instructions.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Savon_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "reg:mdt_practice",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:4c7a01d84c"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends reporting access times using THL guidance Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions with handover alerts, since the Health Care Act sets no maximum time for cancer suspicion, the STM roadmap (measure 3.1.2) plans national pathways and access times for five cancers by 2026–2028, and the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "law:no_max",
          "q:ed87906241",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends a KYS-style referral template, a persistent-symptoms referral rule after a normal X-ray—already in the KYS regional pathway document, addressing the mentor insight that weak referrals get lower urgency—and a named diagnostic-phase contact, as no regional pathway document names a diagnostic contact and the STM roadmap (measure 1.2.3) plans coordinator guidance by 2026–2028 for county adoption by 2029–2031.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:only_kys_xray",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
